2026-10-09T19:46:11.1062579Z   PR_BODY_JSON: "Closes #1622\n\nEngineering scope currently refuses additional coordination namespaces and exact helpers explicitly declared by the actual reviewed issue. This accepts those literal declarations with exact-file versus trailing-slash directory semantics, retains the branch namespace fallback and unconditional research/geography exclusions, and carries the same validated actual issue declarations through the linked reader and verified canonical reservation to normal combined integration. The issue-file CLI requires a single valid bounded engineering work block, open engineering issue and matching PR issue number. No hardcoded issue/PR exceptions, ownership expansion, workflow or cap changes.\n\nValidation: focused handoff scope and issue claim suites passed on Node v24.19.0, including actual credential-free CLI Git fixtures and adjacent linked/claim readers. Positive controls cover the extra composition namespace, exact helper and branch fallback; adverse controls cover missing/malformed/foreign scope, issue mismatch, unrelated/sibling/exact-file suffixes, duplicate/unsafe broad roots, traversal/globs and all research/geography exclusions. The first attempt retains its test typo and missing sparse gate-input failures; both were corrected before the passing run. Local evidence validator reports bytes-verified.\n\nImmutable source baseline: d416ec3fa35b94d114aa42bd858317504e50923f. Manifest: coordination/engineering/engineering-owned-scope-routing-20261009/evidence-quality.json. Original modified files, actual issue snapshots, claim/readiness, passing log and initial failures are inventoried. No GIS/science or large application build ran locally; these code controls establish routing only. Independent exact-head review, normal hosted checks and serialized combined queue/readback/cleanup remain required. No geographic/source approval, selected activation, provider, deployment or production action.\n\nAfter normal integration, #1523/PR1621 can retry the normal shared scope path against its unchanged actual reviewed declarations. Parent #1202 and its geographic/source obligations remain open with their owners.\n"
